-## Subtopics
-
-### DeSplat
-Focuses on deblurring and handling motion blur in dynamic scenes, whereas STG focuses on explicit temporal modeling of Gaussian parameters [12925-desplat.md].
-
-### 360 Gaussian Splatting
-Addresses omnidirectional or wide-baseline dynamic scenes, while STG is optimized for multi-view video setups with specific temporal polynomial modeling [12929-360-gaussian-splatting.md].
-
-### Data Compression and Storage Optimization
-General techniques for reducing model size, whereas STG achieves compactness through feature dimensionality reduction (9 vs 48 params) and polynomial motion [12943-data-compression-and-storage-optimization.md].
-
-### Bézier-boundary gradient approximation
-Uses Bézier curves for boundary handling, distinct from STG's polynomial trajectory for motion [13137-b-zier-boundary-gradient-approximation.md].
-
-### Discontinuity-aware Gaussian Splatting
-Handles geometric discontinuities explicitly, while STG relies on temporal opacity for emerging/vanishing content [13138-discontinuity-aware-gaussian-splatting.md].
-
-### SOGS
-Uses second-order anchors for optimization, whereas STG uses first-order polynomial coefficients for motion [13171-sogs-second-order-anchor-for-advanced-3d-gaussian-splatting.md].
-
-### TraGraph-GS
-Uses graph-based temporal consistency, while STG uses parametric polynomials [14454-tragraph-gs.md].
-
-### Optimization Schedule and Densification
-General densification strategies; STG adds guided sampling for sparse areas [15107-optimization-schedule-and-densification.md].
-
-### 3D Gaussian Splatting Training Loop
-The base loop; STG extends it with temporal parameters and guided sampling [15139-3d-gaussian-splatting-training-loop.md].
-
-### Scene Representation and Geometry Constraints
-Adds geometry losses; STG focuses on appearance and motion [15421-scene-representation-and-geometry-constraints.md].
-
-### Perceptual Wrapper
-Adds perceptual losses; STG uses D-SSIM [15438-perceptual-wrapper.md].
-
-### TurboGS
-Focuses on rendering acceleration; STG achieves speed via feature MLP and polynomial motion [15697-turbogs.md].
-
-### Error-Guided Sparse Pixel Sampling
-Similar to STG's guided sampling but may differ in depth usage or aggregation [15708-error-guided-sparse-pixel-sampling.md].
-
-### DashGaussian
-Optimizes for streaming; STG is for offline training with real-time rendering [15742-dashgaussian.md].
